Package: drsvyr
Title: Latent Class Segmentation for Complex Survey Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kevin", "Linares", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "kevin.linares@example.org")
Description: A Shiny application that fits a weighted latent class model to a
    battery of survey items on complex survey data, with every standard error
    derived from the survey's own stratified jackknife replicate design.
    Segment prevalences, item-response probabilities and domain estimates are
    all design-based; domain estimates additionally carry a BCH three-step
    correction for classification error. The analyst supplies an SPSS or Stata
    file, makes every substantive choice themselves, and leaves with a
    self-contained report and their data with segment membership added. A
    language model drafts prose at four points and never touches a number.
